{# Status badge — pass/fail/warning/neutral indicator.

   SCOPE: outcomes that already happened — SPF/DKIM auth results, message
   disposition (what a receiver DID to a message), and connection health. Here
   `quarantine`/`reject` mean mail was held back or refused, so the amber/red
   tones are correct.

   NOT for a domain's published DMARC policy. Policy runs the opposite way:
   `p=reject` is full enforcement and the best available posture. Use
   `<twig:PolicyBadge>`, which scales severity by exposure instead of by
   outcome. #}
{% props status, label = null %}

{% set badgeClass = {
    'pass': 'badge-success',
    'fail': 'badge-error',
    'softfail': 'badge-warning',
    'warning': 'badge-warning',
    'neutral': 'badge-ghost',
    'none': 'badge-ghost',
    'temperror': 'badge-warning',
    'permerror': 'badge-error',
    'quarantine': 'badge-warning',
    'reject': 'badge-error',
    'active': 'badge-success',
    'error': 'badge-error',
    'inactive': 'badge-ghost',
}[status] ?? 'badge-ghost' %}

<span class="badge badge-sm {{ badgeClass }}">{{ label ?? status }}</span>
